  #line-at(52.44pt, 549.79pt, "Fig. 5. (a) Simulated electric-field distribution along the vertical direction ")
  #line-at(52.44pt, 558.91pt, "of the β-Ga₂O₃ device at applied biases of 100, 300, 400, and 425 V. (b) ")
  #line-at(52.44pt, 568.15pt, "Corresponding impact-ionization generation rate profiles, showing a ")
  #line-at(52.44pt, 577.27pt, "pronounced increase in generation at 400 V and above. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(56.88pt, 591.82pt, "As shown in Fig. 5(a), the electric field increases ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 603.34pt, "monotonically with the applied bias and reaches peak values ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 614.86pt, "exceeding 1.5 MV/cm near the contact region at 400 V and 425 ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 626.38pt, "V, while gradually decreasing across the bulk of the substrate. ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 637.78pt, "Correspondingly, the simulated impact-ionization generation ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 649.3pt, "rate, as shown in Fig. 5(b), increases by several orders of ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 660.82pt, "magnitude at these biases, reaching peak values on the order of ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 672.34pt, "10¹⁶–10¹")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(80.904pt, 668.86pt, "8")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(84.144pt, 672.34pt, " cm⁻³·s⁻¹. Although the impact generation is spatially ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 683.86pt, "localized near the high-field region, it provides an additional ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 695.256pt, "carrier multiplication pathway that enhances the overall ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 706.776pt, "photocurrent at high bias. These results indicate that avalanche ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 718.296pt, "multiplication contributes to the observed high-gain regime ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 59.76pt, "under CW illumination, acting in conjunction with bulk ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 71.28pt, "photoconductive transport mechanisms. ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(402.07pt, 89.66pt, "IV.")
  #line-at(421.51pt, 89.66pt, "C")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(428.71pt, 89.66pt, "ONCLUSION")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(323.35pt, 101.18pt, "This letter presented the first experimental demonstration of ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 112.7pt, "nonlinear photoconductive gain operation in β-Ga₂O₃ devices ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 124.1pt, "under CW visible-light excitation. By employing a thin ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 135.62pt, "nitrogen-doped insulating epilayer on a conductive substrate, ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 147.14pt, "high electric fields were achieved at reduced operating voltages, ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 158.66pt, "enabling a transition from linear photoconduction to a high-gain ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 170.18pt, "regime at ~0.67 MV/cm. The resulting photocurrent exhibits an ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 181.7pt, "approximately 20-time enhancement relative to the linear ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 193.1pt, "regime, with peak values approaching 475 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(492.46pt, 193.1pt, "µ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(498.22pt, 193.1pt, "A. Experimental ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 204.62pt, "transient measurements and TCAD simulations together ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 216.14pt, "suggest that this gain arises from the combined effects of trap-")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 227.66pt, "assisted transport and localized impact ionization. These results ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 239.18pt, "demonstrate the feasibility of visible-light-triggered β-Ga₂O₃ ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 250.73pt, "device for compact, high-field photoconductive detection ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 262.13pt, "applications without the need for deep-ultraviolet optical ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 273.65pt, "sources. ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
